1. She has social anxiety and took drama classes in school to overcome it. (Verbatim: "I chose drama so I could learn to not be mute and face my social anxiety")
2. She regrets not choosing computer-related subjects in school despite loving computers. (Verbatim: "I always thought that was a big mistake because I was like oh no I can't do anything computer like")
3. She initially believed doors to her desired career were locked, but later realized they were always open. (Verbatim: "I thought those doors were locked and they weren't locked no no no no no no they're not")
4. She studied science at university, not computer science, despite her interest in technology. (Verbatim: "I picked science and the science um and I was so scared for the longest time that I wouldn't be able to like get into it")
5. Her childhood dream was to make people happy. (Verbatim: "my dream my answer when I was little though was just to make people happy")
6. She worked as a developer for a financial company but felt unfulfilled. (Verbatim: "when I was being a developer then I don't know like for a financial company working on that stuff I just didn't feel very happy")
7. She believes knowledge from her education remains valuable even when not directly applied. (Verbatim: "the knowledge is still in my brain it's not like it poofs because I do something slightly unrelated")
8. She values doing what makes her happy and believes it opens more opportunities. (Verbatim: "just go for what makes me happy and what opens the most doors")
9. She considers herself a law-abiding citizen and opposes piracy. (Verbatim: "I'm not a pirate I'm not I'm a law-abiding citizen")
10. She uses Crunchyroll and High Dive to track anime releases. (Verbatim: "I use things like Crunchyroll and High Dive") [end of text]



1. She is passionate about anime and enjoys discussing it extensively. (Verbatim: "I find it really fun to talk about anime it's something i'm really passionate about")
