1. She has experience working in IT support and development. (Verbatim: "I used to do a lot of it support and development and stuff like that")
2. She finds it frustrating when companies avoid upgrading outdated systems despite technical issues. (Verbatim: "they'd be like okay but like can you fix it in a way that doesn't involve me spending money to upgrade it")
3. She has encountered servers so slow that software installations took an entire day. (Verbatim: "sometimes it would take me like the whole day")
4. She has had to install software on underpowered devices like laptops and Microsoft Surface tablets. (Verbatim: "they were so slow that sometimes it would take me like the whole day")
5. She has faced skepticism due to her age and gender in professional IT settings. (Verbatim: "because i'd be younger and a girl they'd normally ask for another opinion because they'd be like this girl doesn't know anything")
6. She enjoys watching anime, particularly isekai genre, which she refers to as "junk food" for her viewing habits. (Verbatim: "i can't resist isekai trash okay okay it's my junk food i need it")
7. She is critical of second seasons in anime due to the pressure to live up to the first season. (Verbatim: "the problem with us that's an issue i think that will always be associated with sequels is that a sequel has to live up to its first season")
8. She appreciates when second seasons surpass the quality of the first season. (Verbatim: "sometimes you get these lovely gems that where the second season ends up being better than the first season")
9. She is aware of corporate mindset in media production where sequels are made for profit rather than passion. (Verbatim: "they can be like well it's guaranteed to make us money because the first season is already there so there's no pressure to even make this one good")
10. She finds certain anime tropes, like "harem" plots, unappealing due to lack of self-insertion appeal as a woman. (Verbatim: "the problem with harms is i feel like harms are designed for you to self-insert yourself into the main character but like i'm not a guy so i don't really self-insert myself as a guy") [end of text]



